Package: RAssistant
Title: A Lightweight AI Assistant for RStudio
Version: 0.21.0
Authors@R: person("MySimpleSmart", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "120612480+MySimpleSmart@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Opens the existing Source-aware chat assistant in the RStudio
    Viewer. Supports image uploads, optional live console context, contextual R help,
    a project Knowledge Base (PDFs, notes, R examples and custom instructions),
    reviewed Source edits and explicitly approved script validation. Stores optional credentials
    in the operating system credential store, separately from package updates.
License: file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports:
    askpass,
    callr,
    codetools,
    commonmark,
    ellmer (>= 0.5.0),
    htmltools,
    httpuv,
    jsonlite,
    keyring (>= 1.3.0),
    knitr,
    later,
    remotes,
    rlang,
    rstudioapi,
    shiny (>= 1.14.0)
Suggests:
    httr2,
    pdftools
URL: https://github.com/MySimpleSmart/RAssistant
BugReports: https://github.com/MySimpleSmart/RAssistant/issues
Config/RAssistant/Changes: Turn Send into Stop while waiting for an AI response, using a centered square icon and the existing button style. Keep the draft and attachments ready for a deliberate retry.
    Run provider requests in a separate R process so Stop can terminate a pending HTTP request. Discard cancelled or stale responses and cancel pending work when the Viewer session closes; pass credentials through a private pipe.
    Allow stopping AI analysis after an approved script run while keeping its execution output. Mark stopped context receipts clearly and preserve existing Source edit and execution approvals.
